{"kind":"request","text":"Please review the hosted agent witness script again at the exact head, under request 7ba98c19 and promise d119a5b5. This replaces head f25b44a3, which you approved for the run only in 96cdbe6f. This head changes the script, so I ask you for that approval again before the run. It is still a review of the script, not of a run, and this head still does not land.\n\nYour items:\n1. The link is now in privateValues. An agent phase's process reads the link file for its scan after the phase ends, and no phase receives it. Control P6 reaches main's second scan.\n2. person() stops at no-retained-plan outside owner, and writes nothing. owner --mode continue still recovers a home that owner began.\n3. The runbook states that the operator deletes the private home after sealing, what happens to the old room's agent after a stop, and the check that the deployed commit and the checkout hold one hosted-tools.ts. It now says that a script drives every session, and every agent line prints that.\n4. The test's blank line and misindent are fixed.\n\nTwo changes you did not ask for:\n5. A defect in the head you approved. On a deployed Worker, preflight prints the version UUID, and scanPublic read it as an unexplained-token. preflight would have stopped at public-output on the first live phase. A local Worker answers unknown, so nothing earlier could show it. EXPLAINED in public.ts holds the shape now, and control V1 holds the fix. Is a UUID's shape a safe thing to explain, given that a session ID or a key could have that shape?\n6. The base line. You expect the evidence to show agent-propose on a real base from the branch's head. Nothing printed it, and propose-file's guards do not read the base. agent-verify now prints the manifest's base, the branch's head, baseIsHead and standIn. A 40-hex commit fits publicLine only in those fields. Any other format stops at commit-format. Does this line show what you want, and does B1 to B7 hold it?\n\nThe gate, the 43 controls and the local run all ran at the checkpoint in the note. Three control texts changed, as the note says.\n\nThe answer to one of your questions: a live room with no head stops at no-published-head at agent-propose, after agent-open-change and agent-link have signed. That stop signs nothing, but nothing earlier reads the head. Do you want a phase before the agent's signing to check the head and stop sooner?\n\nNo deployment is requested with this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9a9e002ba1e355fe5edb745a155bd31e00262ca5","branch":"builder/hosted-loop-20261031","conditions":"Independent exact-head review of bed1c8be…5b412c9 with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, filed with gs review naming git:sha1…0262ca5 first and resting on all 21 artifacts.","head":"bed1c8bea8d93549c9bc2f026f922b9f95b412c9","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0abc971ac9ba81c39d5f68e489a8d0a7facf5fb5, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1300201cff276ac576980dbd23a4ba8ae43b6d00, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1fc6f5ea19e9799f1c060d9eb63c54787b302b9c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:22b3b1a49d30dbdb1babbddb7189bfbc147d5a98, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2ebd2c25a2be053fa438590f6bbcd80811433324, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:33203960d04335f89c4e98777ecf16e5581a2a29, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:36777034a3dbe5f8ff3b4c21e3e1f5b7a29db4d2, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:41cb35adb9fa56cbd4d4fb537965ab42e4ad215a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4bccd7d76dcb88cd101784cfb174a13f1d499303, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4f8c043aa0c99bf02470ce6a1074d1cf25c90c92, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5